42	     *
43	     * Laravel's own firstOrCreate retry re-reads with a consistent snapshot, which under
44	     * REPEATABLE READ can miss the row a sibling transaction just committed and rethrow the
45	     * 1062. A locking read is a current read, so it always sees the latest committed row; this
46	     * is what stops a duplicate observation from failing the host's building-queue processor.
